{"kind":"event","event_id":7684,"event_uid":"01M2P8YMPCBX2KQ2D0JWCAC8S7","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":326,"issue_uid":"01M2P8CPSB719RJ7MRWTPFF6YQ","issue_short_id":"f6yq","actor":"engine:run-169","hlc_physical_ms":1789601469132,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"dfa2c7fb23b9d225d02d750f47a0edeaf23a210771327ba02e71552cbf178efe","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2P8YMPAMWDXFQC7XQGDSM6H","author":"engine:run-169","body":"{\"kind\":\"driver:attention\",\"task\":\"1\",\"attention\":\"needs-human\",\"msg\":\"session ended without hand-off\",\"actor\":\"\",\"id\":\"01M2P8YMPD0000W17284959SMT\",\"ts\":1789601469133}","created_at":"2026-09-16T23:31:09.130982382Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T23:31:09.132Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":7685,"event_uid":"01M2P97F9X0CKP2T4D8D2X669B","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":326,"issue_uid":"01M2P8CPSB719RJ7MRWTPFF6YQ","issue_short_id":"f6yq","actor":"exam:1@run-169","hlc_physical_ms":1789601758525,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"b6cb901e5a6876fff4e6865848204ce30cd35dd4e10777c44ec2fd52cbcaef03","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2P97F9TTQ8ZZASKZ1TK1JKM","author":"exam:1@run-169","body":"examiner (run-169 task 1), exam handed in — both guarded sims written, red at BASE, green under a reference implementation.\n\nWhere each leg is answered:\n- `fleet/tests/test_run_engine_state_exams.mjs`, new section at the bottom under a banner naming this task: run-169 (a) [M1] `stateExamStemsOf`, the Proof's five-entry list → `['buy-milk','pin-todo','probe']` plus `['a_test.sh']`/`[]`/`undefined` → `[]` (and `null` and a bare string, the same clause's 'a non-array'); (b) [M2] one record seeded `real` killed / `rig` survived / `other` killed, then `['real']` → one row, `['real','other']` → `other, real`, and `[]` / `'real'` / no third argument → the same three rows `other, real, rig` deep-equal on all eight keys, plus `['ghost']` → `[]`; (f) [M2] the fifth `Run:` over both sims' bytes.\n- `fleet/tests/test_run_engine_review_economy.mjs`, same: (c), (d), (g) [M3] through `rig(...)` and (e) [M4] over the two documents.\n\nTwo readings a later session would otherwise have to reconstruct:\n\n1. MEASURED, and it contradicts the plan's Context: an `exam:` arm that returns WITHOUT writing does not leave the run 'as the existing legs do'. `handoffExam` sets `examBlobs` to `[[landing, null]]`, which is truthy, so `examRunnable` is true, the exam command runs against the absent file and exits 127; the task takes its one repair round and parks `failed` / `proof-red` before any review round, which makes leg (c)'s skip unreachable for a reason that is not this task's claim. Keeping `testCmd: 'bash a_test.sh'` beside `proofTests: ['tests/state-exams/real.test.ts']` has the same end, because the landing is under the reserved directory and `a_test.sh` is never handed to the graded clone. So the three runs are arranged as: `testCmd` names the Proof path itself (the driver rewrites it to the landing), and the `exam:` arm writes an exam that exits 0 at whatever the driver's own `EXAM PATHS:` line gives — the pre-review pass then really executes the exam and is green (`driver:exam-run` `[[0, 0]]`, no `fix:` round), which is the pass the skip requires. Each run asserts that arrangement as a named sim precondition, so a later drift fails saying so rather than failing a graded leg. The `exam is green at BASE` judgment call this produces gates nothing. Leg (d) keeps `proofTests: ['a_test.sh']` with `testCmd: 'bash a_test.sh'` and a green `a_test.sh`, which is the existing legs' own shape.\n\n2. Leg (g)'s prompt half is not vacuous and was measured at BASE: hollow findings reach the reviewer prompt as `- receipt <id> driver:finding [...] read: hollow: <stem> ...` lines, so at BASE that prompt carries `hollow: rig` and the assertion is a real red. The leg also asserts the prompt DOES carry `hollow: real`, so an engine that stopped briefing the referee on findings at all cannot pass it silently.\n\n3. Leg (e) [M4] grades the two `Run:` greps hard, and the placement hard — CONTRACT.md's occurrence must sit in the bullet carrying the `every mutant killed` rule, report-format.md's in the one `tasks[].stateExams` table row. M4's substance is graded as two READINGS rather than a wording: the sentence carrying `tests/state-exams/` must name the Proof, and the prose must say what a task with none of those paths reads (`every stem`/`whole directory`/`whole record`/`entire …`, alternation). Both were checked non-vacuous against BASE's bytes: neither document says `Proof` in that prose today, and none of the fallback alternatives occurs in either. A prose edit that says what M4 asks in any ordinary phrasing passes; the exam does not pin a spelling.\n\nVerified: at BASE `test_run_engine_state_exams.mjs` stops at run-169 (a) with `stateExamStemsOf … Got: undefined` (the absent `Produces:` export — a namespace import is used so the missing export is an assertion rather than a link-time SyntaxError that would hide the legs below), and `test_run_engine_review_economy.mjs` stops at the first graded assertion of (c) with the unscoped record's `hollow: rig` finding; every sim precondition in both files passes at BASE. Against a scratch reference implementation (`stateExamStemsOf`, the third argument on `stateExamRowsOf`/`stateExamsOf`, and the two call sites — the review round's `stateExamRowsOf(runDirAbs, task.id, stateExamStemsOf(proofTests))` and the report row's `stateExamsOf(runDirAbs, r.task, stateExamStemsOf(WAVES.flat().find(...).proofTests))`) plus a draft of the two doc sentences, both sims print ALL TESTS PASSED. Nothing is unsatisfiable; `fleet/run-engine.mjs` and the two documents are untouched in this tree.","created_at":"2026-09-16T23:35:58.522676756Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T23:35:58.525Z"}
